{title: Twice as Much as Before}
{subtitle: Job 42:10–13; 42:14; 42:15; 42:16–17}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Cm7] | [Abmaj7] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
When [Eb]Job prayed for his friends he [Bb/D]stood
The [Cm7]Lord restored his fortunes to his [Gm]hand
[Ab]He gave him twice as much as [Eb]before
A new begin[Cm7]ning after the war [Bb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
His [Eb]brothers and sisters came to his [Bb/D]door
They ate [Cm7]in his house and felt the floor [Gm]
They [Ab]consoled him over the trouble [Eb]he saw
Giving [Cm7]pieces of silver [Bb]and gold rings to draw
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He named the [Eb]first Jemimah
The [Bb]second Keziah
And the third [Cm]K-eren-hap-puch
A [Ab]beauty that is [Bb]much
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]Nowhere in all the land were they [Bb/D]found
[Cm7]Women as beautiful without a [Gm]sound
[Ab]In Job's daughters the light did [Eb]break
With an in[Cm7]heritance for their [Bb]sake
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He named the [Eb]first Jemimah
The [Bb]second Keziah
And the third [Cm]K-eren-hap-puch
A [Ab]beauty that is [Bb]much [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
They re[Ab]ceived an inheritance among [Bb]their brothers
A [Eb]gift of jus[Bb/D]tice and [Cm7]gentle glories
The [Ab]latter part of his life was [Bb]blessed
[Ab]More than the first and never [Bb]less
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Ab]He saw his children to the [Bb]fourth generation
And died old and full of [Eb]days
{end_of_verse}
